  "diary": "The day’s true movement lay not in the garden, but in the ledger. I walked Lodhi Gardens to cool my head, but the heat of the contradiction remained. The Directorate’s register has made a dead professor into a Joint Secretary. At first, I treated this as a mere slip of the pen, an error of the sign awaiting correction. But as I reviewed the vouchers and Ramesh’s conflicting notes on the dhobi’s bill, the distinction became clear: the state’s signs are not external marks but internal determinations. The error is not just wrong; it is an institutional fact. The state’s money and authority proceed on these names. To correct it, I must work through the contradiction, not merely erase the ink. Ramesh stood at the table, keeping his distance, a small mirror of the bureaucratic hierarchy I study. He is polite, yet rigid. I asked him to sit; he sat for a minute. The house is quiet now. The file waits. The owl spreads its wings as dusk falls, but the thought inside it is still sharp. I will sleep, and Monday the Notion will be tested.",
